From e64832354652ba0e09eed73629e26a7ba655470b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:29:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/ssi: the Rotary G/R/B/Y Click; mikroBUS AN as a digital
 pin

click-rotary is the Rotary Click's two 74HC595 (the LED ring) with its
EC12D encoder and push switch: quadrature on PWM and AN, A = B at each
of the 30 detents, A leading clockwise, 1 ms per edge; the switch drives
INT high while pressed. Sockets gain AN as a digital pin (an_pin) for
it; a Click may now have four outputs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
