diff --git a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
index 4a544d6..ae546fc 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
@@ -155,6 +155,16 @@ headers, so one UART Click at a time; it then takes SERCOM3's place in
   ``speed-ckn``, ``course-cdeg``; the date and time come from the RTC
   (``-rtc``).
 
+``rotaryg``, ``rotaryr``, ``rotaryb``, ``rotaryy``
+  Rotary G/R/B/Y Click (v100): a ring of 16 LEDs on two 74HC595 (LATCH on
+  CS with R19 4.7 kOhm pull-down, MR# on RST with R18 4.7 kOhm pull-up;
+  ``outputs`` bit n lights LED n+1, LED1 at six o'clock, clockwise) and an
+  EC12D incremental encoder (``click-rotary``): A on PWM, B on AN used as a
+  digital pin (R25/R24 10 kOhm pull-downs), 30 detents a turn with A = B
+  at each, A leading clockwise, 1 ms per edge; the push switch on INT
+  drives high while pressed and floats otherwise (no pull on the Click).
+  QOM properties ``position`` (detents, clockwise up) and ``pressed``.
+
 SPI Clicks on both headers share the SPI bus; each listens only while its
 own CS is low (or, for the 74HC595 and MAX7219, latches on its own CS).
 
